        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 24 at 1:37PM MST until September 24 at 3:30PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is
expected.

* WHERE...Southeastern Pinal County in southeastern Arizona...

* WHEN...Until 330 PM MST.

* IMPACTS...Dangerous flows over low-water crossings. Some low-water
crossings may become impassable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 137 PM MST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. This will cause small stream flooding. Between 0.4
and 0.7 inches of rain have fallen.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Oracle and Campo Bonito.
- This includes Route 77 between mile markers 98 and 107.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.</instruction>
